  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes with the 3 new regression tests (5 of 5).\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected or throwing job never gave its slot back, so `running` stayed too high and the queue eventually stalled. Every job now frees its slot and starts the next one whether it succeeds, rejects, or throws synchronously. Its own promise still rejects as before.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also waits for `running` to reach 0.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled, so `resume()` with concurrency 4 starts four jobs.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover each of these: failures (async and sync) not stalling the queue, `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs, and `resume()` filling all four slots.",
